<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">York, Maine</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gorgeana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">York is a town on the southern coast of Maine, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, settled by the English in the 1630s as Agamenticus. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinando-gorges">Sir Ferdinando Gorges</a> chartered it in 1641 as the city of Gorgeana, the first chartered English city in America. Massachusetts reorganised it as the town of York in 1652, and it was devastated in a French and Wabanaki raid in 1692.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/york-maine.jpg" alt="York, Maine" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Old_Wilcox_Tavern,_Church_%26_Courthouse,_York,_ME.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>New Jersey is named after the island: in 1664 the Duke of <b>York</b> granted the land to Sir George Carteret, a Jerseyman who had held the island for the Stuarts.</blockquote><a href="/empire/bailiwick-of-jersey">Bailiwick of Jersey · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>It was renamed New York after the Duke of <b>York</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/september-8">8 September in history</a></li><li><blockquote>A Cayuga Nation survives in New <b>York</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/cayuga-nation">Cayuga Nation</a></li><li><blockquote>Today there are Oneida nations in New <b>York</b>, Wisconsin and Ontario.</blockquote><a href="/state/oneida-nation">Oneida Nation</a></li><li><blockquote>Fishing stations and small settlements grew along the coast at Kittery, <b>York</b> and Saco, and in 1639 a royal charter made Gorges proprietor of the Province of Maine.</blockquote><a href="/state/province-of-maine">Province of Maine</a></li><li><blockquote>A large landholding elite owned Hudson Valley manors, and New <b>York</b> City grew as a trading port with many enslaved Africans.</blockquote><a href="/state/province-of-new-york">Province of New York</a></li></ul></section>
